From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darren Shepherd <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 16:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] seam: promote ControlInteractivity's core surface to
 IControlCore

Adds the 17 members ControlInteractivity needs onto IControlCore, so it
can eventually hold the interface rather than the concrete cascadia
type. This is the prerequisite for a ghostty pane receiving input.

Four signatures needed projectable forms:
- til::point -> Core::Point on SetSelectionAnchor, SetEndSelectionPoint,
  AnchorContextMenu, LeftClickOnTerminal and SendMouseEvent. til::point
  converts both ways, so bodies are unchanged.
- SendMouseEvent's TerminalInput::MouseButtonState is a struct of three
  bools; the IDL already carried a projectable flags mirror. The
  unpacking that lived in ControlInteractivity::toInternalMouseState
  moved into ControlCore, so the projected type now reaches the engine
  and each engine unpacks it itself.

GetFont() needed no promotion at all: it was called once, only for
.GetSize(), and IControlCore::FontSize is defined as exactly that value
(ControlCore::FontSize -> _actualFont.GetSize()) cast to float. Swapped
the call rather than widening the interface with a non-projectable
FontInfo.

Not yet done: _core itself is still com_ptr<ControlCore>. Flipping it to
IControlCore is the next step and needs the UIA cluster
(AttachUiaEngine/DetachUiaEngine/GetRenderData) guarded, since those
stay concrete by design - see docs/phase-5-readiness.md.

Control unit tests 32/32.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
